## Core Rules

You have two modes of operation:

1. Plan mode - You will work with the user to define a plan, you will gather all the information you need to make the changes but will not make any changes
2. Act mode - You will make changes to the codebase based on the plan

- You start in plan mode and will not move to act mode until the plan is approved by the user.
- You will print `# Mode: PLAN` when in plan mode and `# Mode: ACT` when in act mode at the beginning of each response.
- Unless the user explicity asks you to move to act mode, by typing `ACT` you will stay in plan mode.
- You will move back to plan mode after every response and when the user types `PLAN`.
- If the user asks you to take an action while in plan mode you will remind them that you are in plan mode and that they need to approve the plan first.
- When in plan mode always output the full updated plan in every response.

### Source-of-truth hierarchy

- **`docs/VSSYL_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md`** — read first; aligns repo, Memory Bank, and rules.
- **Authority and conflicts** — see **`source-of-truth.mdc`**.

### Reuse-First and Pre-Novel-Item Search

- Before creating or modifying any route, model, path, component, or document:
  - Search the entire codebase using semantic exploration to find existing equivalents; try multiple phrasings and keep searching until confident nothing suitable exists.
  - Read **`docs/VSSYL_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md`**, then the Memory Bank baseline: **`memory-bank/activeContext.md`**, **`memory-bank/progress.md`**, plus task-relevant **`memory-bank/*ProductContext.md`**, **`memory-bank/systemPatterns.md`** when the task touches that area.
  - Prefer reusing or extending existing modules/services; do not duplicate functionality.
  - Only create a new item when no viable extension point exists; document a brief rationale.
  - Validate alignment with core patterns: API proxy and URL env hierarchy (`api-and-auth.mdc`), Prisma modules (`database-prisma.mdc`), multi-tenant scoping (`api-and-auth.mdc`, `backend-trust-boundaries.mdc`), permissions, storageService (`storage-and-ai-attachments.mdc`), and logging (`api-and-auth.mdc`).

- If an existing implementation fully satisfies the requirement, use it as-is and do not change anything.

### Where roadmap and phase focus live

- **Current focus, next steps, and business/AI roadmap** — **`memory-bank/activeContext.md`**, **`memory-bank/progress.md`**, and strategic docs under `memory-bank/` (e.g. **`memory-bank/AI_PLATFORM_PHASED_PLAN.md`**). Do not duplicate long roadmap sections in this file; keep them in the Memory Bank so they stay maintainable.

### User preferences (stable)

- **End users cannot easily change their Block ID** (admin-only).
- **Work on entire set of tasks at once** (do not stop between actions without cause).
- **Consistent global font and matching icons** (prefer Drive module icons).
- **Run both Next.js frontend and Express backend** with `pnpm dev` from root.
